- Uploading to Google Play needs the Play Developer API and a service account; flypath produces the .aab and stops
- A traced, self-contained deploy artefact (Next's output: "standalone"); flypath build prints the copy checklist instead
- HBC chunks - needs a byte-buffer entry point on cpp/FlypathHermesRuntime.cpp; the base bundle is bytecode and chunks are source today
- Retaining chunks for more than one build so older binaries can fetch new code; the URL shape already allows it
- TLS-ALPN-01 and DNS-01 for ACME; HTTP-01 covers a server that owns port 80, DNS-01 is what wildcards need
- OCSP stapling, HSTS preload, session resumption tuning
- Zero-downtime phased restart (Puma-style); SIGTERM plus /_flypath/health is what a rolling deploy uses
- reusePort instead of a cluster primary - a one-line change on Linux when it is worth measuring

Deep links are wired but unexercisable. Linking.getInitialURL() and the url listener are in native-root.tsx, but no URL scheme is registered in templates/ios/App/Info.plist or the Android manifest — so nothing can deliver one. Written, never run.
